<article class="env-lemma" id="0GM4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GM4">Lemma <span data-tag="0GM4">13.27.9</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $K$ be an object of $D^ b(\mathcal{A})$ such that $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ p_\mathcal {A}(H^ i(K), H^ j(K)) = 0$ for all $p \geq 2$ and $i > j$. Then $K$ is isomorphic to the direct sum of its cohomologies: $K \cong \bigoplus H^ i(K)[-i]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose $a, b$ such that $H^ i(K) = 0$ for $i \not\in [a, b]$. We will prove the lemma by induction on $b - a$. If $b - a \leq 0$, then the result is clear. If $b - a > 0$, then we look at the distinguished triangle of truncations 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \tau _{\leq b - 1}K \to K \to H^ b(K)[-b] \to (\tau _{\leq b - 1}K)[1]  \]
</div>
    <p>
       see Remark <a href="/tag/08J5" data-tag="08J5">13.12.4</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/05QT" data-tag="05QT">13.4.11</a> if the last arrow is zero, then $K \cong \tau _{\leq b - 1}K \oplus H^ b(K)[-b]$ and we win by induction. Again using induction we see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(\mathcal{A})}(H^ b(K)[-b], (\tau _{\leq b - 1}K)[1]) = \bigoplus \nolimits _{i < b} \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}^{b - i + 1}(H^ b(K), H^ i(K))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       By assumption the direct sum is zero and the proof is complete. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>